Z||000000||Silver88GT||10-16-2001||06:57 PM||||I've been following the Forum religiously since I bought my first Fiero in July and you guys have helped me out a bunch.  I am hoping you can come through again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The fan for the heat and ac has only worked intermittently from day one.  I works, but not until the car has run for 5-10 minutes.  Not a big deal until the colder weather came and I couldn't see until I was halfway to where I was going.<P>I replaced the blower motor with one from the boneyard and things were fine for a week or so until the problem started again.  This time I tried 3 different switchs (again used) and none made a difference.  Fuse is fine.  Visible wiring looks fine.  What next?<P>I know there are some switches or sensors or something in the system as well.  Could these be the problem?  Anyone else have this happen?  I've searched other posts and most of the Fiero repair sites.  <P>Hope someone can help.  I'd rather be spending my limited Fiero time making it more fun, not more comfortable.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Silver88GT||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||10-16-2001||07:17 PM||||Check the connections on the plug that goes into the blower motor - sounds like there could be some corrosion in there.||||reg||1
