Z||000003||Silver88GT||10-16-2001||11:43 PM||||Phil, all the connections look like new. <P>Could it be the high speed blower relay or the blower resistors?  What happens when these are bad?  If it is not them, I may just get a NEW blower and see if that works.<P>Philphine, have not been in Louisville for a while, so it wasn't me you saw.  If there is ever any Fiero get togethers in Louisville though, let us know,  I'll come over and bring my buddy with a yellow Formula.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick86GT||10-17-2001||06:43 PM||||Silver,<BR>If the blower is intermittent at all speeds, then the resistors and high speed relay are not the problem.  <P>Check it when it's not working: test for power to the blower. If you show 12 volts power at the blower (purple wire), but no operation, temporarily run a separate ground wire from the blower ground (black wire) back to the neg. battery terminal to determine if you have a bad ground or a bad motor. <P>If you show no voltage at the blower motor, well, you've changed the switch and checked the fuse...the power distribution system is next to check. Look at the fusible link connections near the battery for corrosion.<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Silver88GT||10-18-2001||09:32 PM||||Patrick, thanks.  I do have power to the motor and I checked the ground and it appears OK.  Bad motor, right?<P>Well, stopped by Autozone and got a new motor since this one from the salvage yard didn't seem to work out too well.  Put it in and NOTHING!  Same problem.  <P>Ground is fine.  Power at the fuse box and at the motor.  Fuse is fine.  Tried 3 differnt switches.  I'm stumped (and getting pi**ed)!<P>Unless anyone has any other ideas, I guess I'll have to take it to my auto electric guy.  He can always figure this stuff out.  It's been running a little rough lately anyway.  No codes, but acts like the oxygen sensor.  With all the stuff I am having to replace on the 2.8, I can't afford not to go 3.1 or 3.4 when its motor swap time.  ||||reg||1
